  "text": "[calm] The player is a single web page that never navigates — the estate's projection room. Its stage frames the estate's real rooms, served live. [short pause] A chapter's script is two tables sharing one clock. The narration's words, each stamped with the millisecond it is spoken. And the actions, each pinned to a word's time. At this word, frame the aquarium. At that word, pull a lever. [short pause] Like this: on the next sentence, the room behind me changes. [pause] Now. [short pause] No editor made that cut. A line in a table did — and it makes the same cut for anyone who presses play.",
